			"Message": "chore(Deps/Editor): Sync Microsoft pointer to 41bac285 with Agent Host refactor and MCP security hardening\n\nAdvance the Microsoft VS Code Editor dependency submodule from 87a1679c to 41bac285 to integrate upstream stability fixes, security enhancements, and architecture refactorings.\n\nKey upstream changes incorporated:\n- Agent Host Refactor: Replace legacy `AgentHostEditingSession` with a direct external edit progress part, decoupling file edit rendering from the editing session.\n- Session State Migration: Introduce a one-way URI state migration mechanism (`legacyResource`) to preserve user state during provider URI shape changes.\n- MCP Security: Store MCP OAuth client secrets in OS secret storage instead of plain-text `mcp.json` files.\n- Security Hardening: Add path traversal rejection in the Create Workspace file tree and sanitize unsafe node names.\n- Agent Host Lifecycle: Fix SSH reconnect failures after sleep/network changes with periodic backstops and auto-resume logic.\n- UI Enhancements: Add rich hover interactions for session titlebars and enable the Agents window by default for Insiders builds.\n\nNo source changes in the Land application — pure submodule pointer update to keep the dependency tree aligned with the latest upstream VS Code security and architecture improvements.\n\nRefs: microsoft/vscode",
			"SHA": "ed34d13e925dfddb48234c4ac31bd5dbf877609e"
		}
